@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo FOLLOWED BY A SPACE OR THE END OF THE LINE, AND THAT IS
rem CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN BY A WHOLE-WORD MATCH. P19-ARCH-001's copy had a
rem line beginning "remrem" that a prefix match let through; cmd ran it as a
rem command and printed "not recognized" to stderr. This copy fixes the line
rem and the check.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P19-DATA-001 CFD ANALYSIS DATA MODEL. The exact invocation, recorded so the
rem run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, FIFTY-TWO in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem   launch.cmd           git hash-object f11039e6dc366d7c469a15cf74fb3867fd5ffeff
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units at full
rem parallelism exhausted the commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens
rem nothing. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT THIS MILESTONE ADDS. Two identities in core (CfdAnalysisId, a document
rem object, and CfdBoundaryConditionId), three headers and three translation
rem units in src/cfd (CfdData, CfdAnalysisObject, CfdResult), the boundary
rem condition records, the definition, its semantic fingerprint, the result
rem source, the result, the failure, the slot and the state machine; one test
rem file, one compile-fail group, ADR-061 and the zero-match groups. Because
rem core's Id.hpp changed, every module recompiles.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. unit.Cfd selects the new data cases and
rem the boundary cases; unit.Thermal and unit.Structural the two modules whose
rem identities sit beside the new ones in Id.hpp; unit.Linalg and the mesh-side
rem groups as before; unit.P18Qualification the final gates; refmod. the
rem reference suite; the CLIs that share a driver; architecture. every
rem ownership gate.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION. It is in the full
rem ctest of every preset.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
rem
rem THIS RUN HAPPENS ON THE HASIB MACHINE, as every milestone since P17-CLI-001,
rem by the owner's decision of 2026-10-14. GCC 16.1.0 WinLibs POSIX UCRT r4,
rem the CMake 4.4.1 and Ninja it bundles, and the dependency prefix built by
rem deps/CMakeLists.txt from the same hash-verified archives: Qt 6.11.2, OCCT
rem 8.0.1, zlib 1.3.1, Netgen 6.2.2604. The machine-specific cache values
rem (build root, dependency prefix, FetchContent source directories) were
rem configured for P17-CLI-001; qualify.cmd's plain `cmake --preset` reuses them.
rem
rem BEFORE LAUNCHING, the OneDrive client's memory is checked: P19-ARCH-001's
rem first attempt lost its debug link to a OneDrive process holding 56 GB.
rem
rem THE FRESHNESS HALF of the fresh-binary proof (the binaries are newer than
rem the clean and than the newest source) is done by postrun-data.ps1, after
rem the run.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Linalg|unit\.Structural|unit\.Cfd|unit\.Thermal|unit\.P18Qualification|unit\.P17Qualification|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\.|cli\.thermal\.|cli\.structural\.|cli\.mesh\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
